   "html_text": "What would social arrangements that distribute benefits and burdens fairly between individuals look like exactly? An immediate problem when debating what a just society looks like is that individuals tend to be partial. The wealthy will likely argue in favor of a scheme of justice that allows them to keep their wealth, for instance. They may portray the contingent condition of the propertyless as an expression of their inferior talent or merit and justify a limited access to societal positions a",
